{"strongs": "H2552", "word": "חָמַם", "translit": "cha.mam", "root": "חמם", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb", "gloss": "be or become warm", "definition": "[ חָמַם ] verb be or become warm (Late Hebrew id. , Pi`el, make warm , Aramaic , חֲמַם be warm ; Arabic become hot , of water; also heat, kindle fire in ) — Qal Perfect חַם Ps 39:4 ; Exod 16:21 וְחַם consecutive 1Kgs 1:2 ; Eccl 4:11 חַמּוֺתִ֫י Isa 44:16 Imperfect יָחֹם Isa 44:16 וַיָּ֫חָם 2Kgs 4:34 ; Isa 44:15 also יִחַם 1Kgs 1:1 יֵחַם Deut 19:6 יֵחָ֑ם Eccl 4:11 3 feminine singular תֵּחַם Ezek 24:11 יֵחַמּוּ Hos 7:7 וַיֶּחֱמוּ Gen 30:39 וַיֵּחַמְנָה v Gen 30:38 (last seven forms could be also from יחם q. v.; but no decisive evidence that this √ is used in Qal; they are placed under חמם by Thes Ew § 193 a Ol § 243 b ; see also Kö i. 365, 417 ff. , who on account of יחם Pi`el Infinitive Gen 30:41 ; Gen 31:10 , derives last two, needlessly, from יחם ); Infinitive לַחְמָם Isa 47:14 , compare Job 30:4 (where, however, ׳ ל is from לֶחֶם Mich Di unless ( Luzz Che ) we read לְחַמֵּם Pi`el Infinitive in both); חֹם 1Sam 11:9 ; Hag 1:6 ; Neh 7:3 suffix חֻמּוֺ Job 6:17 חֻמָּם Jer 51:39 — 1. literally, be or grow warm Exod 16:21 ( P ; subject שֶׁמֶשׁ ), compare 1Sam 11:9 ; Neh 7:3 and Job 6:17 (suffix of impersonal subject); from fire Isa 44:15 ; Isa 44:16 (twice in verse); Isa 47:14 (compare above); natural heat 1Kgs 1:1 ; 1Kgs 1:2 (by personal contact), so 2Kgs 4:34 ; Eccl 4:11 (twice in verse), from clothing Hag 1:6 of Jerusalem under figure of pot or caldron Ezek 24:11 . 2. figurative, subject לִבִּי Ps 39:4 (|| בַהֲגִיגִי תִבְעַראֵֿשׁ ), compare Deut 19:6 of conspirators Hos 7:7 Chaldeans Jer 51:39 . 3. of heat in conception (animals) Gen 30:38 ; Gen 30:39 (compare יחם ). Niph`al Participle נֵחָמִים באלים Isa 57:5 ( Kö i. 371 ), inflame oneself with , of idolatry. Pi`el Imperfect 3 feminine singular תְּחַמֵּם Job 39:14 keep eggs warm (of ostrich). Hithpa`el Imperfect יִתְחַמָּם warm oneself Job 31:20 מִגֵּז כְּבָשִׂים by means of fleece of sheep.", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2862')\">BDB2862</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2552')\">H2552</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2861')\">BDB2861</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2863')\">BDB2863</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>חָמַם</bdbheb>] <b>verb</b> <highlightword>be or become warm</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>, Pi`el, <highlight>make warm</highlight>, Aramaic <placeholder1806/>, <bdbheb>חֲמַם</bdbheb> <highlight>be warm</highlight>; Arabic <placeholder1807/> <highlight>become hot</highlight>, of water; also <highlight>heat, kindle fire in</highlight>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>Qal</b> <highlight>Perfect</highlight> <bdbheb>חַם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 39:4\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"39\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"39\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(19,39,4)\">Ps 39:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 16:21\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"16\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"16\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(2,16,21)\">Exod 16:21</ref> <bdbheb>וְחַם</bdbheb> consecutive <ref ref=\"1Kgs 1:2\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(11,1,2)\">1Kgs 1:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"Eccl 4:11\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(21,4,11)\">Eccl 4:11</ref> <bdbheb>חַמּוֺתִ֫י</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 44:16\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,16)\">Isa 44:16</ref> <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> <bdbheb>יָחֹם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 44:16\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,16)\">Isa 44:16</ref> <bdbheb>וַיָּ֫חָם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Kgs 4:34\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(12,4,34)\">2Kgs 4:34</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 44:15\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"44\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"44\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(23,44,15)\">Isa 44:15</ref> also <bdbheb>יִחַם</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 1:1\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"1\"